WEBVTT

00:04.800 --> 00:06.760
A house call for the Empress?

00:06.760 --> 00:08.430
Is something wrong with Her Majesty?

00:08.900 --> 00:11.270
Her condition apparently took a sudden turn.

00:11.270 --> 00:12.770
We'll go and—

00:15.070 --> 00:17.330
<i>I don't like the sound of that cough...</i>

00:19.110 --> 00:19.800
What's wrong?

00:20.150 --> 00:21.200
Nothing!

00:21.200 --> 00:24.340
What sort of illness does Her Majesty have?

00:24.340 --> 00:26.820
I cannot speak of it here.

00:26.820 --> 00:28.250
Go get ready.

00:29.600 --> 00:30.460
Yes, Father.

00:53.490 --> 00:59.960
<b>Parallel World Pharmacy</b>

02:00.970 --> 02:05.220
<b>Episode 3</b>

02:14.930 --> 02:16.070
Archduke!

02:16.400 --> 02:17.590
Head Court Physician.

02:18.730 --> 02:20.480
How is Her Majesty's condition?

02:20.480 --> 02:21.760
It does not look good.

02:22.330 --> 02:25.090
Her lungs appear to have
weakened considerably.

02:47.280 --> 02:50.290
Your Majesty, I am sorry to disturb you.

02:52.980 --> 02:54.640
<i>So this...</i>

02:54.640 --> 02:56.060
<i>is this nation's empress,</i>

02:56.060 --> 02:58.190
<i>Her Majesty Élisabeth II.</i>

03:05.480 --> 03:07.080
Farma, my bag.

03:07.080 --> 03:08.090
Y-Yes, sir.

03:28.680 --> 03:29.690
<i>And this...</i>

03:29.690 --> 03:31.790
<i>is how examinations are performed here?</i>

03:44.080 --> 03:46.590
I see. Then it's as we feared...

03:46.590 --> 03:49.530
Indeed. The stars are in a horrible state.

03:50.230 --> 03:53.450
I'm afraid her destiny is near its end.

03:54.440 --> 03:56.790
<i>Did he just mention </i>stars<i>?!</i>

03:56.790 --> 04:00.020
Nevertheless, I shall continue
what treatment I can.

04:00.020 --> 04:01.830
Farma, assist me.

04:01.830 --> 04:03.010
Y-Yes, sir.

04:04.060 --> 04:05.500
"Treatment..."

04:09.350 --> 04:13.030
<i>In this world, pharmacians have
independent prescribing authority,</i>

04:13.260 --> 04:15.850
<i>so they both prescribe
and compound medicine.</i>

04:16.410 --> 04:18.890
<i>The smell of opium and mandrake.</i>

04:18.890 --> 04:20.300
<i>Anesthetic effects.</i>

04:20.800 --> 04:23.030
<i>So he created an anesthesia potion?</i>

04:25.070 --> 04:28.190
Your Majesty, how are you feeling?

04:30.140 --> 04:31.300
Bruno,

04:31.660 --> 04:33.980
speak plainly.

04:33.980 --> 04:36.710
Am I beyond recovery?

04:37.330 --> 04:39.320
Not at all, Your Majesty.

04:39.620 --> 04:42.290
I have brought a powerful medicine.

04:42.870 --> 04:44.590
Please inhale these vapors.

04:44.590 --> 04:46.700
It should ease your breathing.

04:51.720 --> 04:55.400
<i>With that medicine, no improvement
in her illness can be expected.</i>

04:55.400 --> 04:59.180
<i>So all they can do is lessen
her present suffering?</i>

05:00.830 --> 05:02.160
Call the priest.

05:02.520 --> 05:04.610
Most likely, tomorrow night
will be the critical juncture.

05:07.270 --> 05:10.030
<i>This is like a ritual for euthanasia!</i>

05:10.340 --> 05:12.250
<i>Do they not intend to cure her?</i>

05:12.800 --> 05:13.990
<i>No one here does?</i>

05:15.910 --> 05:17.660
<i>I can't remain...</i>

05:17.660 --> 05:18.710
<i>on the sidelines!</i>

05:29.930 --> 05:31.020
<i>Lung cancer.</i>

05:31.020 --> 05:32.680
<i>Bronchiectasis.</i>

05:32.680 --> 05:33.620
<i>Pneumonia.</i>

05:34.940 --> 05:36.880
<i>It's not simply pneumonia...</i>

05:37.280 --> 05:38.090
<i>In that case...</i>

05:38.360 --> 05:39.550
<i>tuberculosis?</i>

05:42.080 --> 05:44.520
<i>The white death, as it was once known.</i>

05:46.800 --> 05:50.470
<i>Given the lack of injection devices,
the oral route is my only option.</i>

05:50.470 --> 05:52.070
<i>Four medicines, if possible.</i>

05:52.070 --> 05:55.140
<i>One of those four needs to be rifampin,</i>

05:55.670 --> 05:59.150
<i>but it has a high molecular
weight and a complex structure,</i>

05:59.150 --> 06:01.150
<i>making it difficult to envision accurately.</i>

06:02.410 --> 06:04.150
<i>If I mess up...</i>

06:07.540 --> 06:11.790
<i>So this is what it means to deal
directly with the patient.</i>

06:14.470 --> 06:16.180
Mother!

06:15.580 --> 06:16.640
Your Highness!

06:17.010 --> 06:18.260
Prince Louis!

06:18.260 --> 06:21.720
Mother, when will you be all better?

06:21.720 --> 06:22.480
Louis...

06:22.710 --> 06:25.460
Your Highness, we mustn't
disturb Her Majesty!

06:25.460 --> 06:26.070
No!

06:26.310 --> 06:27.130
Your Highness.

06:27.130 --> 06:28.280
No!

07:08.820 --> 07:09.780
Your Majesty.

07:12.180 --> 07:16.750
Though it is not my place, may I request
permission to treat Your Majesty?

07:17.270 --> 07:20.200
There is a new medicine
for Your Majesty's illness.

07:21.270 --> 07:22.670
Farma, stop!

07:23.040 --> 07:24.880
A new... medicine?

07:24.880 --> 07:27.220
Is there... truly?

07:27.220 --> 07:28.120
Yes.

07:28.120 --> 07:31.600
This is no time for jests, boy! Enough!

07:31.600 --> 07:33.300
Hold, Bruno!

07:37.470 --> 07:38.970
You know of a medicine?

07:38.970 --> 07:40.580
That is to say,

07:40.580 --> 07:43.500
you know the name of my affliction as well?

07:44.040 --> 07:45.390
I believe I do.

07:46.870 --> 07:48.130
I see.

07:48.130 --> 07:49.440
Very well, then.

07:49.440 --> 07:50.270
Your Majesty!

07:52.070 --> 07:53.200
Claude...

07:55.510 --> 07:57.770
When I was hale and hearty,

07:57.770 --> 08:01.020
I was held to be the finest practitioner
of Divine Arts in the empire.

08:01.020 --> 08:06.000
I believe I still retain the ability
to discern who is worthy of trust.

08:09.460 --> 08:10.920
You...

08:10.920 --> 08:15.140
I see that you alone...
have not yet given up.

08:16.440 --> 08:17.600
Yes, Your Majesty.

08:17.600 --> 08:20.370
Good. Permission granted.

08:26.930 --> 08:29.130
Farma! Open this door!

08:29.130 --> 08:30.440
What are you doing?

08:30.660 --> 08:33.190
Open up, you fool!

08:44.000 --> 08:47.380
<i>To prevent the bacteria from
acquiring drug resistance,</i>

08:47.380 --> 08:51.420
<i>I need to use three or four
drugs together, if possible.</i>

08:51.660 --> 08:52.930
<i>Isoniazid,</i>

08:52.930 --> 08:54.120
<i>pyrazinamide,</i>

08:54.480 --> 08:55.810
<i>ethambutol,</i>

08:59.970 --> 09:01.320
<i>and finally,</i>

09:01.750 --> 09:03.090
<i>rifampin!</i>

09:31.490 --> 09:32.460
Farma.

09:33.450 --> 09:35.110
What are you doing?

09:37.330 --> 09:39.490
I am preparing for Her Majesty's treatment.

09:39.490 --> 09:40.710
Don't be ridiculous!

09:40.710 --> 09:43.300
No one in the world can
cure the white death!

09:44.450 --> 09:46.110
I'm surprised.

09:46.110 --> 09:48.530
So you had already ascertained
that it was the white death?

09:48.530 --> 09:51.470
That much has been clear
for quite some time!

09:52.360 --> 09:56.940
<i>Unlike me, he diagnosed her
without special help.</i>

09:57.910 --> 10:00.290
<i>He really is a magnificent pharmacian.</i>

10:01.070 --> 10:04.840
Being a pharmacian is not about
pointlessly brandishing your knowledge.

10:05.310 --> 10:09.580
You must use your knowledge
to soothe the patient's heart.

10:10.880 --> 10:14.000
Farma, think of the patient!

10:14.500 --> 10:16.700
The white death is an incurable illness.

10:17.220 --> 10:19.250
The patient is suffering.

10:19.250 --> 10:21.740
What is the point of
driving them to despair?

10:21.740 --> 10:23.810
A new medicine?

10:23.810 --> 10:26.930
To spout such nonsense is reprehensible.

10:26.930 --> 10:29.390
No, Father. The medicine exists!

10:30.190 --> 10:31.340
And it's...

10:31.340 --> 10:33.550
something you need to take as well!

10:38.540 --> 10:40.460
Wait! What are you doing?

10:47.080 --> 10:48.160
Why?

10:49.260 --> 10:50.860
Answer me, Farma!

10:51.420 --> 10:54.840
What is it that you are
attempting to compound?

10:54.840 --> 10:56.750
Put your wand away, Father!

10:56.750 --> 10:59.300
Do you mean to destroy the whole lab?

10:59.490 --> 11:00.550
Answer!

11:00.550 --> 11:03.730
If you cannot explain, it's poison!

11:04.820 --> 11:06.440
Sword Dance of Ice!

11:19.530 --> 11:21.530
What? With no wand or incantation?!

11:22.770 --> 11:23.840
Farma...

11:24.250 --> 11:25.110
No...

11:25.520 --> 11:26.760
Who...

11:27.030 --> 11:28.340
are you?

11:35.150 --> 11:36.870
I ask you once more.

11:36.870 --> 11:38.920
Just who are you?

11:54.760 --> 11:56.500
What is all this?

11:57.740 --> 12:00.250
Knowledge of new medicines.

12:00.250 --> 12:02.790
I dreamed of it the day
I was struck by lightning.

12:05.410 --> 12:06.650
A dream...

12:07.230 --> 12:08.930
And that day was the turning point?

12:09.560 --> 12:10.360
Yes.

12:12.340 --> 12:15.530
On your shoulder. That's the holy mark.

12:15.890 --> 12:17.990
Did the Panactheos grant you a revelation?

12:18.410 --> 12:20.640
I... couldn't say.

12:22.630 --> 12:24.470
So that's the situation.

12:24.470 --> 12:26.440
This is incredible.

12:26.440 --> 12:30.170
To think the Panactheos
granted my son a blessing...

12:30.380 --> 12:32.320
Please, Father!

12:32.320 --> 12:34.650
Administer this medicine to Her Majesty!

12:34.950 --> 12:37.240
If we say that you compounded it,

12:37.240 --> 12:39.450
your standing within the
court will be preserved.

12:41.820 --> 12:42.730
No.

12:45.290 --> 12:49.170
The medicine you make is yours to give.

12:49.480 --> 12:53.220
That has always been my teaching.

12:55.460 --> 12:58.610
Her Majesty placed her faith
in you and your assessment.

12:58.610 --> 13:02.130
She resolved to stake her life
on your medicine.

13:02.130 --> 13:06.840
Thus you, too, must stake your own life
on giving your medicine.

13:06.840 --> 13:10.760
That is a pharmacian's duty,
and a pharmacian's pride.

13:12.780 --> 13:13.960
Yes, Father.

13:22.390 --> 13:24.790
<i>Farma's attribute was positive water.</i>

13:24.790 --> 13:29.360
<i>Even if he can produce water,
he should not be able to erase it...</i>

13:45.720 --> 13:47.130
Are you...

13:48.390 --> 13:51.320
Are you... Farma?

13:51.880 --> 13:54.920
Are you really my son?

13:56.610 --> 14:00.310
I mean, I consider myself to be.

14:08.400 --> 14:10.660
Ladies and gentlemen, sorry for the wait.

14:11.600 --> 14:13.890
Why is he hiding his face?

14:13.890 --> 14:16.660
What disrespect he shows the Empress!

14:16.660 --> 14:18.250
Does it mean he can't face her?

14:18.250 --> 14:19.590
That took some time.

14:19.590 --> 14:22.370
Where is your father?
Did he turn tail and flee?

14:22.690 --> 14:25.350
No. Nothing of the sort.

14:28.370 --> 14:31.290
The time is of no import. Come closer.

14:39.310 --> 14:41.860
This is the new medicine, Your Majesty.

14:45.180 --> 14:49.110
Chief Royal Pharmacian,
shouldn't you stop your son?

14:49.640 --> 14:50.780
No...

14:51.080 --> 14:57.010
He... His skills may have
already surpassed ours.

14:57.370 --> 14:59.500
All I can do is watch him.

15:03.650 --> 15:06.660
Before I report the effects
of this new medicine,

15:06.660 --> 15:08.950
there is something I would
like Your Majesty to see.

15:09.310 --> 15:11.760
Might I have Your Majesty's cooperation?

15:12.960 --> 15:15.890
Very well. Proceed.

15:17.660 --> 15:21.530
This is a sputum sample
I obtained from Your Majesty.

15:25.950 --> 15:30.370
Please bring that close to your eye and
peer through the hole toward some light.

15:33.990 --> 15:35.700
Like this?

15:48.640 --> 15:50.530
What are these?

15:50.970 --> 15:55.180
I see... They look like creatures—

15:59.210 --> 16:00.180
Claude.

16:07.530 --> 16:08.640
Pardon me.

16:10.940 --> 16:11.950
Now then.

16:13.700 --> 16:16.000
What are these?! Bugs?

16:16.330 --> 16:19.160
Head Court Physician, what do you see?

16:20.660 --> 16:23.840
Incredible... They look
just like caterpillars.

16:23.840 --> 16:26.120
Are these living organisms?

16:26.120 --> 16:29.910
Farma, explain what we have witnessed.

16:29.910 --> 16:33.590
They're extremely small organisms
that cause the white death.

16:33.590 --> 16:34.840
They're bacteria.

16:35.130 --> 16:39.560
Your Majesty's body is being
affected by these organisms.

16:39.560 --> 16:41.970
Bac-teria, you say?

16:43.500 --> 16:49.490
There exist diseases in this world caused by
infection with micro-organisms like these.

16:50.340 --> 16:53.080
The medicine I am giving Your Majesty

16:53.080 --> 16:55.920
operates on the organisms
that cause the white death.

16:56.290 --> 17:00.240
If the medicine is taken properly for
half a year, full recovery can be expected.

17:00.510 --> 17:02.450
That is quite a long time.

17:02.450 --> 17:05.300
The white death is a tenacious malady.

17:08.350 --> 17:15.500
Farma, your explanation fundamentally
upends our existing concept of disease.

17:16.270 --> 17:19.850
Very well. I shall take your medicine.

17:21.160 --> 17:22.070
As you wish.

17:27.480 --> 17:30.470
Now then, starting today,

17:30.470 --> 17:33.450
I will watch Your Majesty take
this medicine every day.

17:33.450 --> 17:38.740
This is called directly observed
treatment, short-course—

17:39.690 --> 17:40.600
Your Majesty.

17:41.710 --> 17:45.070
I put myself in your care, Farma.

17:45.680 --> 17:49.290
Your Majesty, I, Farma de Médicis,

17:49.290 --> 17:51.160
hereby stake my life

17:51.160 --> 17:54.290
on Your Majesty's safe
and effective treatment.

17:55.910 --> 17:56.710
Here I go.

18:03.750 --> 18:04.900
Your Majesty.

18:05.280 --> 18:06.230
Yes.

18:15.560 --> 18:16.700
Ladies and gentlemen,

18:17.520 --> 18:22.740
when this new medicine has succeeded in
appropriately eliminating the bacteria,

18:22.740 --> 18:25.570
the white death shall cease
to be an incurable disease!

18:26.250 --> 18:30.200
Never again shall we fear this illness!

18:32.720 --> 18:35.730
Young man, just what is this object?

18:35.730 --> 18:37.740
Please, spare no detail!

18:37.740 --> 18:40.140
What a splendid Divine Art!

18:40.140 --> 18:44.780
This is not a Divine Art.
It is a device anyone can make.

18:44.750 --> 18:47.710
Farma de Médicis...

18:44.780 --> 18:46.840
I will share the designs.

19:16.100 --> 19:18.420
<i>A pharmacian must be close with patients.</i>

19:19.220 --> 19:22.830
<i>What a pharmacian needs most
is not skill, but heart.</i>

19:23.940 --> 19:25.890
<i>In accordance with that conviction,</i>

19:25.890 --> 19:30.840
<i>I have interacted earnestly with my
patients, and I believe I understood them.</i>

19:31.360 --> 19:32.540
<i>And yet,</i>

19:32.540 --> 19:37.210
<i>I have failed to do even a single
fatherly thing for my son.</i>

19:37.930 --> 19:44.490
<i>I don't even know what my son thought
about, or how he felt about his life.</i>

19:49.080 --> 19:54.870
<i>Despite that, I can tell that the boy
before me is not the Farma I knew.</i>

20:04.820 --> 20:08.180
I'm glad Her Majesty managed to sleep.

20:08.180 --> 20:10.340
I hope she rests well.

20:10.640 --> 20:14.480
Y-Yes. I'm sure your medicine helped.

20:15.000 --> 20:16.750
I hope so...

20:23.710 --> 20:25.540
Um, these are for you.

20:27.750 --> 20:31.310
If you're willing to take them, that is.

20:35.490 --> 20:38.160
The Panactheos has blessed you.

20:38.160 --> 20:40.650
A god's will cannot be comprehended,

20:40.650 --> 20:45.110
but I imagine this is a reminder that
I have much room for improvement.

20:47.710 --> 20:51.550
If it is my Guardian Deity's will,
then I can only obey.

20:53.250 --> 20:55.180
You are mistaken.

20:56.330 --> 20:58.210
Though I had knowledge,

20:58.210 --> 21:02.920
I didn't understand the needs of
a patient on the verge of death.

21:03.330 --> 21:06.500
That is something you taught me.

21:07.960 --> 21:10.770
Though I have been granted these abilities,

21:10.770 --> 21:13.180
I am still only an
apprentice-level pharmacian.

21:13.900 --> 21:17.510
My acumen is shallow and unrefined.

21:18.370 --> 21:19.380
So please,

21:19.850 --> 21:22.610
as someone deeply immersed in medicine,

21:22.610 --> 21:25.100
continue to show me the way.

21:25.690 --> 21:28.440
Let's pursue the path of medicine together,

21:28.440 --> 21:29.460
Father.

21:39.270 --> 21:40.280
Thank you,

21:40.730 --> 21:42.100
my son.

23:34.970 --> 23:39.970
<b>Episode 4</b>
